handoff = '''# Metadata3 actual checker source handoff

Source preparation is frozen for different review. No checker definition, main, original utility, target, planned test, Git, PowerShell, FFI or native operation has been executed. Only owned source composition, AST reads and inert new CodeType metadata checks ran.

The selected helper is `review-metadata3-actual006.TEMPLATE.py`, 123091 bytes, SHA256 `02996f245e9ab6e0839e23ce9e9296c40c66bbfecc813a360bb37ce5c874ff8e`. Its fixed runtime role is this same file: future immutable values belong in separately reviewed `ACTUAL_CHECKER_BINDING_001.json`, not in a silently rewritten helper. The source schema is `SOURCE_PROTOCOL_AND_REVIEW_CONTRACT_001.json`; the binding template deliberately contains null future SHA, lease, nonce, coordination and wait selections and cannot be used as an actual binding.

Selected interfaces are final GG6 rev003, M3 final selected corrected005 sources with stable BOUND003 runtime paths, and genuine M3 Source peer002 closed22. The historical owner peer's exact short reviewer `owner_docs_review` is accepted only at its fixed genuine SHA; actual Core reviewers remain canonical `/root/actual_record_checker`. BOUND/LATE reviewer `/root/pubnative_review` must be different. Root owns all producer and unit launch actions.

The metadata checker preserves BEFORE/AFTER typed data guards, current742/config55/Git7/runtime4 pair checks, raw same-API9 stability, original600 lifetime, physical terminal18 versus driver finished20, byte-identical WORK bridge, exact current24 full IDs, bounded complete events and diagnostics, two whole trees only after complete whole proof, Core12 and Whole acceptance7. It adds source closure5, all four PS source bindings, externally selected Root trust8/init8/phase10 source-consistency checks and immutable reviewed argv/output hashes. The source protocol states the proof limits: source-consistent externally Root-correlated tool attribution is not independent OS/tool attestation, Job/descendant/hard deadline or whole-site loaded closure proof.

The retained checker waits on closed fixed create-once tickets and publishes atomic complete Detail followed by Core. Machine PASS follows actual typed data and complete provenance; caller booleans and nominal PASS files do not replace those checks. READY must precede metadata timer start. Root trust selection occurs after genuine Root init tool correlation, then both retained reviewer READY records precede Root's separate metadata GO. Original600, both original ages90 at unit GO, 510 reserve, 450 unit plus after60 and resource60 through spawn remain unchanged. This helper never launches the unit or emits automatic GO.

Nine causal planned tests in `test_metadata3_actual_checker_preparation_001.py` are source-only and UNRUN. They cover strict JSON, identity types and equality sentinels, PS7/Py6 timestamps, closed tickets, chunks and combined caps before reads, complete failure diagnostics, and original freshness. Their SHA256 is `a07f641887fe854d3003c122ad4f7cf5fd0f1a129fa7ff9825a95f602c75df30` (9205 bytes). Any future test loading requires explicitly approved isolated helper scope; no unrun preparation is test acceptance.

Selected old BEFORE006 and AFTER002 originals are retained byte-exact as `original-01.source.bytes` and `original-02.source.bytes`. All intermediate snapshots and one-use metadata composers are history. `FINALIZE_CHECKER_SOURCE_005.py` refused in its own author metadata AST extractor at missing chained assignment OWNER, before checker write; tool4dc93b is preserved in `OWN_FINALIZER005_REFUSAL_001.json`. Distinct finalizer006 corrected only that owned extractor and completed tool5a8158. No spent composer or old actual capture may be replayed.

Next: a different source reviewer must read the complete finite frozen payload, independently audit semantic closure and dependencies, then issue an externally selected actual Source peer. Root must finish independently reviewed actual BOUND source/config/lease/trace bindings. Actual source peer, binding, lease, Root trust selection, READY, tickets, before/after cores, whole proof and unit acceptance remain absent. Author checks are not a source PASS or operational authorization. If a peer finds a defect, preserve this freeze and author a distinct correction; do not mutate historical bytes.
'''
with (OWN / 'HANDOFF.md').open('x', encoding='utf-8', newline='\n') as stream:
    stream.write(handoff)

rows = []
for path in sorted(OWN.iterdir(), key=lambda item: item.name):
    assert path.is_file(), 'owned preparation must have a finite flat payload'
    first = path.read_bytes()
    second = path.read_bytes()
    assert first == second
    rows.append({'path':path.name,'bytes':len(first),'sha256':sha(first)})
